      "content": "Neighborhood-level data points can provide valuable insights into a borrower's propensity for repayment stability. You may consider incorporating metrics such as ($USD) median home appreciation, crime indices (e.g., FBI's Uniform Crime Reporting program), and student enrollment rates at nearby universities. Additionally, data on local employment rates, housing costs, and population demographics (e.g., median rent, income levels) can also be indicative of neighborhood stability. Collecting zip code or census tract-level data can help identify more granular patterns in neighborhood stability.",
