      "role": "user",
      "content": "The density thing is a bit of a jump, but I get what you mean about mobility. My main concern is actually how these metrics might interact with certain types of urban areas. In a lot of the datasets I'm seeing, high turnover and lower residential stability are heavily correlated with certain minority-heavy or lower-income urban corridors. \n\nIf we implement these \"cohesion\" weights, aren't we basically just creating a proxy that penalizes those specific communities? How do you recommend we balance the need for stability metrics without the model essentially redlining these neighborhoods by default?",
